Overlay 0041 (reference 0036 / Ghostship 0032 ported): iOS/visionOS
supersampling — fixes the SUB-NATIVE render trap. LUS's
Fast3dGui::CalculateGameViewport sets mCurDimensions from ImGui's POINT-space
content region, and ImGui::Image upscales that to the native-pixel fb0 — so
every port (this one included) shipped rendering the game SUB-NATIVE
(measured on 2ship: iPhone game render ~1/3 native area; the VP 2D window
sub-native vs its 4K drawable). Scale mCurDimensions to
(native drawable px * ssaa) in StartFrame: ssaa=1.0 alone fixes the upscale
to a 1:1 native present; >1.0 renders above native and downsamples (true
SSAA). Factor is native-px-relative so it lands on native*ssaa whether
mCurDimensions arrives as points or pixels. ONLY mCurDimensions scales —
mNativeDimensions / mGameWindowViewport untouched. Clamped to the backend
max texture size. The visionOS 3D eye override later in StartFrame (overlay
0034) wins in stereo mode, so 3D is unaffected (always true native per eye).
Shell provides SohIos_SsaaFactor (gSohIos.Supersample 1.0-2.0, VP forced
1.0) + SohIos_DrawablePixelWidth. __IOS__-only; macOS build pristine.
Verify: bridge `drawable` cur must equal drawable*ssaa (cur < drawable =
still sub-native).

--- a/libultraship/src/fast/interpreter.cpp
+++ b/libultraship/src/fast/interpreter.cpp
@@ -4382,6 +4382,12 @@
     return false;
 #endif
 }
